{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you err and do not do.</b> Idolatry was included in <b>all the commandments</b> for which the community brings a bull — and now Scripture singles it out here from among them, to be judged by a bull for a burnt-offering and a goat for a sin-offering (Sifrei)." "<b>And when you err, etc.</b> Scripture is speaking of idolatry. Or is it perhaps one of all the commandments? Scripture says <b>all these commandments</b> — one commandment that is like all the commandments: just as one who transgresses all the commandments casts off the yoke and breaks the covenant and shows contempt, so too this commandment — in it one casts off the yoke and breaks the covenant and shows contempt. And which is it? This is idolatry (Sifrei)." "<b>Which YHWH spoke to Moses.</b> \"I am\" and \"You shall have no other gods\" — we heard them from the mouth of the Almighty, as it says (Psalms 62) ״אַחַת דִּבֶּר אֱלֹהִים שְׁתַּיִם זוּ שָׁמָעְנוּ״ (Horiyyot 8a)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :register {:flags {2 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:04.106053673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}